==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃɪməl/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Schimmel.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|gmh|schimel}}, {{m|gmh|schimmel}}, from {{der|de|goh|skimbal||mould}}. The expected Middle High German form is seemingly unattested {{m|gmh||*schimbel}}, but all three forms ({{m|gmh||schimel, schimmel, *schimbel}}) would have yielded modern German ''Schimmel''. Cognate with {{cog|nl|schimmel||mould}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m||-}}

# [[mould]], [[mold]]
# [[mildew]]

=====Declension=====
{{de-decl-noun-m|s|n=sg}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|mildew}} {{l|de|Mehltau}}

=====Related terms=====
{{rel4|de|Blauschimmel|Edelschimmel|Schimmelkäse|schimmeln|Schimmelpilz|schimmelig|verschimmeln}}

===Etymology 2===
Derived from etymology 1 due to the similar colour. At first an attributive construction, seemingly of northern origin, in {{der|de|gml||dat scymelinghe perd}} (1373) and {{inh|de|gmh||ein schemeliges perd}} (1374, [[West Central German]]). {{cog|nl|schimmel||grey horse}} is borrowed from German.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m||Schimmel}}

# a [[grey]] or [[white]] [[horse]]

